  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1508.05 Stormwater Treatment Practices: Gravel Wetlands",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1508.05 Stormwater Treatment Practices: Gravel Wetlands. Gravel wetland systems shall comply with the following:\n\n(a) The system shall be designed in accordance with “UNHSC Subsurface Gravel Wetland Design Specifications”, January 2022, available as noted in Appendix B, unless otherwise specified;\n\n(b) Pretreatment as described in Env-Wq 1508.12 through Env-Wq 1508.16 shall be required when stormwater discharge includes runoff from any source other than pervious surfaces or roof areas;\n\n(c) The system, excluding the saturated zone but including any sediment forebays, shall be designed to completely drain within 72 hours; and\n\n(d) The system shall have 2 treatment bays, each of which is designed to filter at least 45% of the WQV with a minimum flow path of 15 feet, or one treatment bay designed to filter at least 90% of the WQV with a minimum flow path of 30 feet.\n\nSource. #12342, eff 8-15-17 (formerly in Env-Wq 1508.04(f) in #9817-A, eff 12-1-10); ss by #13758, eff 9-28-23; ss by #14472, eff 1-19-26, EXPIRES: 1-19-36; ss by #14656, eff 8-6-26, EXPIRES: 8-6-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html"
